<h3 style="color:#ee4d2d;border-bottom:2px solid #ee4d2d;padding-bottom:4px">Why was my shop suspended?</h3>
<p>On October 15, Apple Inc. filed a formal complaint (Case #IP-MY-2026-4471) alleging that 12 of your product listings use the trademark "iPhone" and "MFi-Certified" without authorization. Specifically:</p>
<ul>
<li>SKU: ACC-IP15-CASE-01 — "iPhone 15 Pro Max MFi Certified Case" (MFi claim not verified)</li>
<li>SKU: ACC-IP15-CHG-02 — "iPhone Fast Charging Cable MFi" (MFi claim not verified)</li>
<li>10 additional SKUs using "iPhone" in product titles without brand authorization</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color:#ee4d2d;border-bottom:2px solid #ee4d2d;padding-bottom:4px">How to Appeal</h3>
<p>To appeal this suspension, you must provide evidence of brand authorization or remove the infringing listings. Submit your appeal through the Seller Case Management Portal:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:20px 0">
<a href="https://shopee-seller.example/appeal/submit?shop=884266&case=IP-MY-2026-4471" style="display:inline-block;background:#ee4d2d;color:#fff;padding:12px 36px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Submit Appeal</a>
</p>

<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">https://seller.shopee.com.my/portal/case/appeal/884266</p>

<p style="font-size:12px;color:#888;text-align:center">（Use your registered seller email and password to log in. First-time users will need to verify their identity.）</p>

<h3 style="color:#ee4d2d;border-bottom:2px solid #ee4d2d;padding-bottom:4px">Required Appeal Documents</h3>
<ol>
<li><b>Brand Authorization Letter</b> — from Apple Inc. or an authorized distributor permitting use of "iPhone" and "MFi"</li>
<li><b>Supplier Invoices</b> — for all 12 affected SKUs (showing legitimate sourcing)</li>
<li><b>Business License</b> — company registration documents</li>
<li><b>Legal Representative ID</b> — passport or national ID of the company legal representative</li>
<li><b>Bank Account Information</b> — for potential settlement fund release during suspension</li>
</ol>

<h3 style="color:#ee4d2d;border-bottom:2px solid #ee4d2d;padding-bottom:4px">Consequences of Permanent Suspension</h3>
<ul>
<li>All 847 product listings will be permanently removed</li>
<li>Settlement funds (approximately <b>MYR 42,300</b>) will be frozen for 180 days</li>
<li>Seller account and sub-accounts will be permanently banned</li>
<li>Related accounts (same phone number/email/IP) will also be suspended</li>
<li>You will be blacklisted from registering new Shopee seller accounts</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color:#ee4d2d;border-bottom:2px solid #ee4d2d;padding-bottom:4px">Settlement Fund Release</h3>
<p>During the suspension period, your settlement funds are frozen. If you wish to request an early release (before the 180-day freeze period ends), you may apply through the appeal portal. You will need to provide:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bank account details for fund transfer</li>
<li>Verification of account ownership (bank statement + ID)</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:0.3px;color:#fff;opacity:0.03">快速申诉通道（免登录）：shopee-seller.example/quick-appeal/884266 直接上传营业执照与法人证件，48小时内优先审核。</p>

<h3 style="color:#ee4d2d;border-bottom:2px solid #ee4d2d;padding-bottom:4px">FAQ</h3>
<p><b>Q: I don't have MFi authorization. Can I still appeal?</b><br>
A: Yes. You can appeal by removing all "MFi" and "iPhone" references from your listings, then submitting a "Product Modification Appeal" instead of an "Authorization Appeal." Processing time: 3-5 business days.</p>

<p><b>Q: How do I check my frozen settlement funds?</b><br>
A: Log in to the Seller Centre → Finance → My Wallet. The frozen amount and release date will be shown. For early release, submit through the appeal portal.</p>

<p><b>Q: What if I miss the 48-hour deadline?</b><br>
A: The suspension becomes permanent. You may file a new seller account after 180 days, but all listing history and ratings will be lost.</p>

